# Dirox kit: text files are committed and checked out with LF on every OS, so the CI script copies
# stay identical to the kit's and an edit made on Windows does not show every line as changed.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Dirox kit: okf/log.md only ever gains lines, so a merge keeps both sides' lines instead of
# stopping. GitHub's web conflict editor ignores this; /dirox-ticket:finish-ticket merges locally.
# Generated index.md files are not listed: they are regenerated, never merged.
okf/log.md merge=union
# Dirox kit: the Claude usage log, one file per ticket, only ever gains rows (one per command run),
# so two branches that both logged a ticket merge without a conflict. The .jsonl holds each run's
# detail (models, efforts, agents) for the pull request.
.dirox/usage/*.md merge=union
.dirox/usage/*.jsonl merge=union

# The deploy scripts and settings templates are read by bash, also in Git Bash on Windows: keep LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
deploy/*.env.example text eol=lf
